--- Root Cause Analysis ---
The build failure is caused by a CORPORATE PROXY / TLS CERTIFICATE issue on
the evaluation workstation (MYTSL01502). The corporate SSL proxy intercepts
HTTPS connections to gitlab.arm.com. Bazel's embedded JVM does not trust the
corporate CA certificate.

This failure is UNRELATED to APM. The same error occurs on a clean checkout
with no APM files present.

Known pre-existing issue — documented in repo memory (bazel-ssl-issue.md).
Resolution requires IT to either:
  1. Whitelist gitlab.arm.com for direct access, OR
  2. Provide a properly installed corporate CA certificate, OR
  3. Configure a corporate proxy in ~/.bazelrc

--- Non-interference Confirmation (Static Analysis) ---
APM files added to tools/ai_sdlc_poc/runtime/apm/:
  .github/instructions/score-ai-sdlc.instructions.md
  .apm/instructions/score-ai-sdlc.instructions.md
  apm.lock.yaml
  apm.yml

Verified via grep — none of the above appear in any BUILD or MODULE.bazel file.
APM files are NOT in any Bazel glob(), filegroup(), or dependency target.
Bazel analysis did reach 446 targets (240 configured) before the SSL failure,
confirming APM files introduced no package-loading or analysis errors.

